@startuml
title Frozen selection: refusal and startup failure
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
actor "Startup" as Host
participant "One native loader" as Loader
participant "Selected provider" as Provider
participant "Machine core" as Core
participant "Management" as Management
Host -> Loader: Both roots + sealed catalogue
Loader -> Loader: Stage separately; verify features and trust\nResolve ties before freezing; retain refusals
Loader -> Loader: Freeze choices; refuse principal conflicts\nShipped conflicts refuse both; never reselect
Loader -> Provider: dlopen chosen image; inspect factory / descriptor
note over Loader, Provider
Initializers may run. Loaded images stay mapped until exit.
No unselected alternative is loaded or retried.
end note
Loader -> Core: Selected contributions + every candidate report
Core -> Core: Validate SDL and authority\nProtect reserved owners; remove missing-owner dependents
alt Rejected before publication
  Core -> Management: REJECTED / INCOMPATIBLE\nNo contribution; affected dependents absent
else Admitted
  Core -> Core: Publish exact schema + digest\nCore, shipped IDs sorted, then other IDs sorted
  Core -> Provider: start
  alt Startup succeeds
    Core -> Management: ACTIVE + selected candidate identity
  else Startup fails
    Core -> Management: FAILED; retain schema and capabilities\nOwn resolutions unavailable; no retry or cascade
  end
end
note over Core, Management
Core management remains available for provider failures.
Selection is not reopened by any branch.
end note
@enduml
